{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789823046488,"sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_a414e5bac1594a9cb44b7d6c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"[\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q01\",\n  \"question\": \"Which statement best defines backing up data?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Creating copies of files and systems so they can be restored if the originals are lost or damaged.\",\n    \"Moving files between network drives to free storage space.\",\n    \"Deleting outdated files to reduce the storage footprint.\",\n    \"Encrypting files so only authorized users can read them.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"Backing up data means creating copies of files and systems so they can be restored if the originals are lost, damaged, or corrupted.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q02\",\n  \"question\": \"Which statement matches a full backup?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Fastest to create and uses the least storage.\",\n    \"Slowest to create and fastest to restore.\",\n    \"Copies only data changed since the last backup.\",\n    \"Creates a continuously updated copy with no version history.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"A full backup is the slowest to create and the fastest to restore, and it uses the most storage.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q03\",\n  \"question\": \"Which statement matches an incremental backup?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Copies all changes since the last full backup.\",\n    \"Creates a real-time copy with no versions.\",\n    \"Copies only data changed since the last backup of any kind.\",\n    \"Restores quickly using only one backup set.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"An incremental backup copies only data that has changed since the last backup, whether full or incremental, and is faster and more storage-efficient.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q04\",\n  \"question\": \"Which statement matches a differential backup?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Copies only data changed since the last backup of any kind.\",\n    \"Creates a continuously updated real-time copy.\",\n    \"Restores slowly because many sets are required.\",\n    \"Copies all data changed since the last full backup.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"A differential backup copies all data changed since the last full backup, so restoring requires only the full backup and the latest differential.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q05\",\n  \"question\": \"Which risk is associated with a mirror backup?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"A deleted source file is also removed from the mirror.\",\n    \"Restore takes longer than incremental backups.\",\n    \"Storage use grows faster than with differentials.\",\n    \"It cannot be restored after a failure.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"A mirror backup does not keep older versions; if a file is deleted from the source, it is also removed from the mirror.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q06\",\n  \"question\": \"Why is a differential backup faster to restore than an incremental one?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"It uses less storage space.\",\n    \"Only the full backup and the latest differential are needed.\",\n    \"It copies less data each day.\",\n    \"It is stored on a separate medium.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"A differential restore needs only two sets, the full backup and the latest differential, while incremental restores may require many sets.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q07\",\n  \"question\": \"What is the goal of the Preparation phase in incident handling?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"To confirm that an incident has occurred.\",\n    \"To notify law enforcement.\",\n    \"To get the organization ready before an incident happens.\",\n    \"To restore systems from backups.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"Preparation is the first phase of incident handling, and its goal is to get the organization ready before an incident happens.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q08\",\n  \"question\": \"Which item is part of the Policies and Plans preparation step?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Preparing a forensic jump kit.\",\n    \"Deploying antivirus software.\",\n    \"Running simulated drills.\",\n    \"Defining Incident Response Team roles.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"Policies and Plans includes establishing an incident response policy, developing an IRP, defining roles such as the Incident Response Team, and setting communication and escalation procedures.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q09\",\n  \"question\": \"Which item belongs to the Tools and Resources preparation step?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Maintaining an updated hardware and software inventory.\",\n    \"Developing an escalation procedure.\",\n    \"Conducting employee awareness training.\",\n    \"Writing the incident response policy.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"Tools and Resources includes deploying security tools, maintaining an updated inventory, preparing a forensic jump kit, and ensuring backup systems are in place and tested.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q10\",\n  \"question\": \"What does the Identification stage accomplish?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"It restores systems from verified backups.\",\n    \"It separates true incidents from false alarms and sets scope and severity.\",\n    \"It assigns owners to corrective actions.\",\n    \"It eradicates malware from affected hosts.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"Identification detects and confirms that an incident occurred, determines scope, nature, and severity, and separates true incidents from false alarms.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q11\",\n  \"question\": \"Which source can indicate a security incident, per the reference?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Payroll records.\",\n    \"Purchase orders.\",\n    \"Alerts from IDS, IPS, and SIEM tools.\",\n    \"Employee vacation schedules.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"Signs of an incident can come from IDS, IPS, antivirus, and SIEM alerts, log analysis, employee reports, and performance anomalies.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q12\",\n  \"question\": \"What is included in the verification steps of Identification?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Containing the affected systems.\",\n    \"Deploying short-term fixes.\",\n    \"Eradicating the root cause.\",\n    \"Documenting findings to preserve chain of custody.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"Verification includes confirming the event is real, gathering initial evidence, classifying the incident type and severity, and documenting findings as discovered for chain of custody.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q13\",\n  \"question\": \"What are the three phases of the response model in the reference?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Notification, response, recovery.\",\n    \"Detection, containment, eradication.\",\n    \"Preparation, identification, recovery.\",\n    \"Containment, eradication, restoration.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"The three-phase response model is Notification, Response, and Recovery.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q14\",\n  \"question\": \"Why should notification lists be prepared before an incident occurs?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"To reduce the number of notifications.\",\n    \"So the right people are reached first time without writing lists mid-crisis.\",\n    \"To keep the incident response team small.\",\n    \"To satisfy insurance requirements.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"Notification lists should be prepared before an incident so teams do not write them from scratch during one; defined communication chains help reach the right people first time.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q15\",\n  \"question\": \"Which group is included in a notification list to assess regulatory obligations?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Affected users and customers.\",\n    \"Internal IT and security teams.\",\n    \"Legal and compliance officers.\",\n    \"Network administrators.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"Legal and compliance officers assess regulatory obligations, liability exposure, and mandatory disclosure requirements.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q16\",\n  \"question\": \"How does timely notification help an organization, per the reference?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"It increases the recovery budget.\",\n    \"It prevents all incidents.\",\n    \"It replaces the need for containment.\",\n    \"It limits the damage before the threat spreads.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"Timely notification limits damage by letting security teams isolate the threat early, meets legal deadlines, preserves trust, and speeds recovery.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q17\",\n  \"question\": \"How should incident reports be kept as new information emerges?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Strictly factual and updated.\",\n    \"Speculative to prompt discussion.\",\n    \"Brief and finalized early.\",\n    \"Shared only after investigation ends.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"Incident reports must be strictly factual and updated as new information emerges, avoiding speculation.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q18\",\n  \"question\": \"Which action belongs to containing an incident?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Restoring data from backups.\",\n    \"Disconnecting compromised devices to stop lateral movement.\",\n    \"Reviewing lessons learned.\",\n    \"Drafting the breach report.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"Containment includes isolating affected systems, disabling compromised accounts, applying short-term fixes, and preserving evidence.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q19\",\n  \"question\": \"Which action is a short-term containment fix, per the reference?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Rebuilding the compromised host.\",\n    \"Updating the incident response plan.\",\n    \"Blocking malicious IPs and closing exploited ports.\",\n    \"Conducting a security scan.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"Short-term fixes include blocking malicious IPs, closing exploited ports, and applying emergency firewall rules.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q20\",\n  \"question\": \"Which activity is part of removing the cause of an incident?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Gradual system rollout.\",\n    \"Stakeholder notifications.\",\n    \"Continuous monitoring.\",\n    \"Eradicating backdoors and unauthorized accounts.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"Removing the cause covers root cause identification, malware eradication including backdoors and unauthorized accounts, closing the vulnerability, and eradication verification.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q21\",\n  \"question\": \"What is a clean restore point?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"A backup taken before the incident, confirmed free of malware.\",\n    \"The most recent backup available.\",\n    \"A backup created after eradication.\",\n    \"The first backup made during setup.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"Recovery uses a clean restore point, a backup taken before the incident and confirmed free of malware or tampering.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q22\",\n  \"question\": \"How should systems be restored after an incident?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"In the order they were attacked.\",\n    \"In priority order based on the organization's recovery priorities.\",\n    \"All at the same time.\",\n    \"From newest to oldest backup.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"Systems are restored in priority order, bringing critical business systems back first according to the organization's recovery priorities.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q23\",\n  \"question\": \"Which step verifies that restored systems work properly before going live?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Obtaining legal approval.\",\n    \"Deleting old logs.\",\n    \"Renewing software licenses.\",\n    \"Running security scans for traces of the threat.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"Testing after restore includes verifying functionality, running security scans to confirm no trace of the threat remains, checking performance, and obtaining sign-off.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q24\",\n  \"question\": \"Which method is suggested for finding the real cause instead of the symptom?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Repeating why until reaching something fixable.\",\n    \"Reviewing the backup policy once.\",\n    \"Asking who is responsible first.\",\n    \"Skipping the symptom analysis.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"The 5 Whys method keeps asking why until you reach something you can actually fix, moving past the symptom.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q25\",\n  \"question\": \"Which two questions judge whether a backup really worked?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"Who made it and where it was stored.\",\n    \"How big it was and how fast it copied.\",\n    \"How much data was lost and how long the organization was down.\",\n    \"Which vendor produced it and its warranty.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"A backup is judged by how much data was lost, which relates to the RPO, and how long the organization was down, which relates to the RTO.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q26\",\n  \"question\": \"What should every finding from a post-incident review have?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"A budget estimate and vendor name.\",\n    \"A person in charge and a due date.\",\n    \"An approved workaround.\",\n    \"A timeline for annual review.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n  \"explanation\": \"Every finding needs a person in charge and a due date, then the response plan, backup policy, and guides are updated.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q27\",\n  \"question\": \"When does incident documentation start, per the reference?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"After the incident is contained.\",\n    \"When the report is requested.\",\n    \"The moment the incident is detected.\",\n    \"During the lessons learned meeting.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"Documentation starts the moment the incident is detected; it is a running log, not something written at the end.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q28\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the incident log be written?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"As a running log of each step with the time while working on the problem.\",\n    \"As a summary written after everything is resolved.\",\n    \"As a report for each department.\",\n    \"As a record of final findings only.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n  \"explanation\": \"Responders write each step with the time while still working on the problem, recording facts only and never guesses.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q29\",\n  \"question\": \"Which statement matches how the incident report is tailored for management?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"The official breach notice filed before the legal deadline.\",\n    \"Plain-language guidance for affected users.\",\n    \"A full technical timeline with root cause and pending fixes.\",\n    \"A short 1 to 2 page summary of cost, downtime, and business impact.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n  \"explanation\": \"Management receives a short 1 to 2 page summary covering cost, downtime, business impact, and what the team needs to prevent recurrence.\"\n},\n{\n  \"id\": \"ch5-q30\",\n  \"question\": \"When does the 72-hour window for notifying the National Privacy Commission begin?\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    \"When the investigation is finished.\",\n    \"When the report is drafted.\",\n    \"When you know or have good reason to believe a breach happened.\",\n    \"When the affected users are contacted.\"\n  ],\n  \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n  \"explanation\": \"Under RA 10173 and NPC Circular 16-03, the 72-hour clock starts when you know or have good reason to believe a breach happened, not when the investigation is finished.\"\n}\n]","filePath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\c5q.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\c5q.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\c5q.json","time":{"start":1789823046455,"end":1789823046484}},"id":"prt_0b9c3e131001HJ3152fgrTcm01","sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","messageID":"msg_0b9c3d161001aqC9d0bQ0haK00"}}
