{"type":"text","timestamp":1789823506757,"sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","part":{"id":"prt_0b9cb1a5f001aXSQh9WKZN21AO","messageID":"msg_0b9cad70c001JKD19SwL92QHbH","sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Produce `questions.json` (one valid JSON object) for an interactive comprehensive exam generator (\"IAS 2 Reviewer\") whose content is grounded in the PDF reference at `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\source.pdf`.\n- The work must follow the loaded skill `interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator` and the workflow embedded in `opencode.log` (chapters ≈30 questions, timed/untimed modes, encyclopedia ≥10 entries, stable IDs, explanation per question, balanced answers, anti-guessing, exact JSON schema, no HTML/markdown output, one-line final reply).\n\n## Important Details\n- Reference material: `C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/enaxqoqxb74s4g/source.txt` (primary source of truth; was missing, so re-extracted from the PDF with PyMuPDF: 28 pages, ~90k chars). Actual content is ITAS311-T Information Assurance and Security 2 reviewer, lesson units L3–L8 (post-audit activities appears twice: L3 + L5).\n- Required schema (from opencode.log): `{ title, subject, summary, chapters:[{chapterId,title,description,questions:[{id,question,choices(4),correctAnswer(0-3),explanation}] }], encyclopedia:[{chapterId,term,definition}] }`. Write ONLY `questions.json`; do not create HTML/CSS/markdown files; do not print the JSON; final reply is a one-line confirmation.\n- `job.json` says `\"title\": \"IAS 2 Reviewer\"`, output = `questions.json`, and `status.json` currently `{\"status\":\"running\",\"message\":\"Generating exam\"}` (should likely be flipped to completed at the end).\n- Chosen chapter structure (merged L3+L5 to avoid duplication): ch1 Post-Audit Activities (42 q), ch2 Log Information and Security Controls (40 q), ch3 Risk Management Process (25 q), ch4 Business Continuity Management (30 q), ch5 Backing Up Data and Application (30 q) = 167 questions; encyclopedias 81 entries.\n- Answer distribution targets (verify after re-merge): ch1 A10/B11/C11/D10; ch2 A10/B10/C10/D10; ch3 A6/B7/C6/D6; ch4 A8/B8/C7/D7; ch5 A8/B7/C8/D7.\n- Anti-guessing length audit is the active concern: unique-longest-correct was ch1 62%, ch2 52%, ch3 44%, ch4 83%, ch5 80% (must drop; fix approach = rewrite choices per flagged question, keeping the same `correctAnswer` index).\n- Python 3.11 at `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python311\\python.exe`; pymupdf 1.28.2 available.\n- No double-quote characters inside JSON strings; apostrophes are fine. Do not alter `correctAnswer` when swapping in fixed choices.\n- Flagged question IDs needing fixes: ch1 all done in fix1.json (q01,q03,q05,q06,q07,q08,q10,q11,q12,q13,q14,q16,q17,q18,q19,q23,q25,q27,q28,q29,q30,q31,q32,q33,q34,q35,q36,q37,q38,q39,q40,q41); ch2 = q01,q02,q03,q04,q05,q06,q07,q08,q09,q11,q14,q18,q19,q20,q21,q23,q24,q25,q26,q27,q32,q33,q34,q36,q37,q39,q40; ch3 = q01,q04,q07,q08,q11,q13,q14,q16,q17,q19,q20,q24,q25; ch4 = q01,q02,q03,q04,q05,q06,q07,q08,q09,q10,q11,q12,q13,q14,q15,q16,q17,q18,q19,q20,q21,q24,q25,q26,q28,q29,q30; ch5 = q01,q02,q03,q05,q06,q07,q08,q09,q10,q11,q12,q13,q14,q16,q18,q19,q20,q21,q22,q23,q24,q25,q27,q28,q29,q30.\n- The rebalanced choice texts for ch2–ch5 were fully drafted during the analysis (correct text kept at the original index), so an agent can re-derive or reuse that plan; each fix is a qid → [4 new choices] mapping in JSON.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Loaded skill `interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator`; read `job.json`, `status.json`, `opencode.log`.\n- Extracted PDF text → `source.txt` (28 pages, 90024 chars) via PyMuPDF; read and analyzed the whole reference (lessons L3–L8).\n- Authored question-bank fragments: `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\c1q.json` (ch1, 42), `c2q.json` (ch2, 40), `c3q.json` (ch3, 25), `c4q.json` (ch4, 30), `c5q.json` (ch5, 30), `enc.json` (81 encyclopedia entries).\n- Wrote `merge.py`; merged and validated `questions.json`: 167 questions, 0 structural errors (4 choices each, correctAnswer 0–3, unique IDs, non-empty Q/explanation), balanced global A/B/C/D = 42/43/42/40.\n- Ran two audits: answer distribution per chapter (matches targets) and length-bias audit revealing the unique-longest-correct leak (62/52/44/83/80%).\n- Wrote the first fix file `fix1.json` (ch1 rebalanced choices, all ~32 entries) and confirmed each new choice list keeps its original `correctAnswer` index.\n\n### Active\n- Authoring remaining fix data files: `fix2.json` (ch2), `fix3.json` (ch3), `fix4.json` (ch4), `fix5.json` (ch5) — new 4-choice arrays, same correct index.\n- Plan: apply fixes (replace `choices` arrays on the fragments), re-run `merge.py`, re-run distribution + unique-longest/shortest audits; then finish status/confirmation. Todo list still shows authoring/merge/validation items in progress.\n\n### Blocked\n- None. (Length-bias fixes are authored-content work, not blocking tooling.)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\fix2.json` (ch2 flagged qids → new choice arrays), then `fix3.json`, `fix4.json`, `fix5.json`, using the drafted rebalanced texts that keep `correctAnswer` unchanged.\n2. Write/run an apply script that reads each fix, replaces `choices` in the matching fragment `cNq.json`, and saves; then run `python \"...\\merge.py\"`.\n3. Re-run the length audit (unique-longest and unique-shortest per chapter) plus answer-distribution check; adjust any residual outliers (target ≤~30% each).\n4. Update `status.json` to completed and reply with the one-line confirmation (no JSON echoed).\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json`: deliverable (currently pre-length-fix version).\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enax