{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789823944326,"sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_2b446dc7330c437284dbb396","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"ch4-q01\": [\"A framework of policies and processes for handling disruptive incidents.\", \"A documented set of procedures followed during a single disruption.\", \"A technical plan for restoring all servers after an outage.\", \"A financial reserve maintained for unexpected business expenses.\"],\n  \"ch4-q02\": [\"A framework of policies for managing daily business operations.\", \"Procedures for keeping critical functions running during a disruption.\", \"A technical plan for restoring data after a system failure.\", \"A yearly schedule for reviewing the continuity program.\"],\n  \"ch4-q03\": [\"An organization-wide continuity management framework.\", \"A set of procedures for keeping functions running during a disruption.\", \"A technical, IT-focused effort to restore systems and data after an outage.\", \"A policy governing employee emergency responses during incidents.\"],\n  \"ch4-q04\": [\"The maximum acceptable amount of data lost.\", \"The time needed to verify restored data sets.\", \"The absolute limit of disruption before survival is threatened.\", \"The maximum acceptable time to restore a business function.\"],\n  \"ch4-q05\": [\"The maximum acceptable amount of data loss as a point in time.\", \"The time needed to resume normal processing after the restoration.\", \"The maximum downtime the business can tolerate or survive.\", \"The minimum service level to be maintained during a disruption.\"],\n  \"ch4-q06\": [\"The preferred recovery target for restoring services.\", \"The absolute limit of disruption an organization can survive.\", \"The average downtime across all past recorded outages.\", \"The budget assigned for continuity investments.\"],\n  \"ch4-q07\": [\"The time needed to restore systems after an outage.\", \"Time lost while waiting for vendor support teams.\", \"Time after restoration to verify data and resume processing.\", \"The time between detection and the formal notification.\"],\n  \"ch4-q08\": [\"By the total amount of media coverage received.\", \"By the number of departments involved.\", \"By the duration of the response effort.\", \"By escalating levels of severity and impact.\"],\n  \"ch4-q09\": [\"The ability to absorb and adapt without losing required function.\", \"The capacity to restore lost data from backup storage sets.\", \"The speed and uptime of the network connection.\", \"The number of backup sites that remain available.\"],\n  \"ch4-q10\": [\"A device that fails during periods of peak system load.\", \"A component whose failure stops the entire process.\", \"A server that has no backup at all.\", \"A process that depends on one external vendor.\"],\n  \"ch4-q11\": [\"Eventual restoration of services only after the disruption.\", \"Reducing the overall cost caused by disruptions.\", \"Sustained delivery of critical services during a disruption.\", \"Timely notification of all the relevant stakeholders.\"],\n  \"ch4-q12\": [\"It is the average downtime across incidents.\", \"It is adjusted automatically after every test.\", \"It is optional for all non-critical business functions.\", \"It is the outer boundary that recovery must stay within.\"],\n  \"ch4-q13\": [\"Financial impact from lost revenue and penalties.\", \"The number of backup locations available.\", \"The size of the continuity team in place.\", \"The type of operating system being deployed.\"],\n  \"ch4-q14\": [\"Because different functions use different software.\", \"Because some functions tolerate more downtime than others.\", \"Because each function is given a separate budget.\", \"Because every function reports to different executives.\"],\n  \"ch4-q15\": [\"It stays constant until the MTD is reached.\", \"It declines as buffers absorb the impact.\", \"It accelerates and compounds the impact over time.\", \"It resets after each recovery milestone.\"],\n  \"ch4-q16\": [\"They each set separate recovery limits unrelated to MTD.\", \"They are measured after normal operations resume.\", \"They replace the need for an MTD entirely.\", \"Their combined values must stay inside the MTD boundary.\"],\n  \"ch4-q17\": [\"Identify the critical processes that cannot be interrupted.\", \"Derive the RTO and RPO targets from the recovery ceiling.\", \"Set the MTD threshold based on the impact analysis.\", \"Model the cumulative impact over multiple time periods.\"],\n  \"ch4-q18\": [\"Consult stakeholders, regulators, and auditors.\", \"Derive RTO and RPO targets inside the ceiling.\", \"Quantify the financial impact over time.\", \"Identify the critical processes first.\"],\n  \"ch4-q19\": [\"A method for ranking project risks by their likelihood.\", \"A financial audit of all recovery investments.\", \"A process to identify and evaluate the effects of a disruption.\", \"A review of the continuity plan's version history.\"],\n  \"ch4-q20\": [\"BIA asks what could go wrong; risk assessment asks recovery speed.\", \"Both answer the same continuity question in different terms.\", \"Risk assessment measures the impact; BIA measures the likelihood.\", \"BIA asks the impact and recovery speed; risk assessment asks what can go wrong.\"],\n  \"ch4-q21\": [\"Minimum Business Continuity Objective (MBCO).\", \"Recovery Time Objective (RTO) time target.\", \"Work Recovery Time (WRT) time target.\", \"Recovery Point Objective (RPO) data target.\"],\n  \"ch4-q24\": [\"Structured interviews and workshops.\", \"Automated network vulnerability scans.\", \"Weekly server backup logs.\", \"Quarterly firewall rule reviews.\"],\n  \"ch4-q25\": [\"Because live testing is too expensive.\", \"Because regulators require regular annual updates.\", \"Because plans drift out of step as conditions change.\", \"Because the plan is written only once.\"],\n  \"ch4-q26\": [\"A change in the weather forecast pattern.\", \"A merger or organizational restructure.\", \"A quarterly departmental marketing report.\", \"A routine staff training session.\"],\n  \"ch4-q28\": [\"To identify and assign new emergency contacts.\", \"To validate assumptions and uncover gaps before an event.\", \"To approve and confirm the annual continuity budget items.\", \"To update the BIA questionnaires and forms.\"],\n  \"ch4-q29\": [\"Plan the testing and exercise approach.\", \"Test the current continuity plan.\", \"Review the test results and findings.\", \"Update the plan with the lessons learned.\"],\n  \"ch4-q30\": [\"MTD is the ceiling each recovery target must fit beneath.\", \"RTO is the ceiling that each target must exceed.\", \"RPO determines the budget set for recovery.\", \"WRT replaces the MTD notion in testing.\"]\n}","filePath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\fix4.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\fix4.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\fix4.json","time":{"start":1789823944305,"end":1789823944322}},"id":"prt_0b9d1eaca001y9X9dQFiKttGJp","sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","messageID":"msg_0b9d1e5f4001yYfSa1ccvtTeJX"}}
