{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824114858,"sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_3e262f66559d4cc580f418fd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"& \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python311\\python.exe\" \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\spotcheck.py\""},"output":"### ch1-q10\r\n Q: In the reference example, what missing item did the audit team address during the exit interview?\r\n   [0] The finance team's reconciled cash position for the quarter.\r\n   [1] The IT department's access control and user log reports.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [2] The network team's revised firewall policy for servers.\r\n   [3] The HR department's hiring records.\r\n EXP: The example shows the audit team identifying that the IT department had not submitted its latest access-control review or user-permission logs, then asking who will provide them and establishing a deadline.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q23\r\n Q: In Step 5, what does interpreting the results require the analyst to determine?\r\n   [0] Which raw files should be deleted after the analysis step.\r\n   [1] What is being learned from the results of the analysis.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [2] Which software performed the analysis fastest.\r\n   [3] Which metrics were collected during Step 2.\r\n EXP: Step 5 asks what you are learning from the results so the insights can be applied to the business.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q24\r\n Q: Which item is a purpose of an audit report?\r\n   [0] Reducing the number of audit findings.\r\n   [1] Assigning blame for control failures.\r\n   [2] Documenting examined evidence.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [3] Automating the audit process.\r\n EXP: The purposes of an audit report include formal communication, documentation of evidence, and initiation of corrective action closure.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q37\r\n Q: Which quality of a good audit report is reflected by issuing the report promptly?\r\n   [0] Confidential.\r\n   [1] Objective.\r\n   [2] Constructive.\r\n   [3] Timeliness.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Timely means the report is issued promptly, one of the six qualities of a good audit report along with accurate, objective, clear, constructive, and confidential.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q39\r\n Q: Which is a disadvantage of presenting audit findings?\r\n   [0] It delays stakeholder acceptance.\r\n   [1] It removes important technical detail.\r\n   [2] It can oversimplify and cause misuse.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [3] It prevents discussion of matters in scope.\r\n EXP: Condensing detailed technical or financial data into summary slides can lead to oversimplification or takeaways taken out of context.\r\n\r\n### ch2-q01\r\n Q: What do security logs record?\r\n   [0] Activity on computers, networks, applications, and devices.\r\n   [1] Approved financial transactions made by senior management.\r\n   [2] The physical location of every employee each working day.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [3] Only the successful logins on a single host system.\r\n EXP: Security logs record activities occurring on computers, networks, applications, and security devices.\r\n\r\n### ch2-q17\r\n Q: How should logs be protected during transmission and storage?\r\n   [0] By encryption.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [1] By compression.\r\n   [2] By duplication.\r\n   [3] By isolation.\r\n EXP: Logs should be encrypted during transmission and storage.\r\n\r\n### ch5-q16\r\n Q: How does timely notification help an organization, per the reference?\r\n   [0] It increases the total recovery budget available.\r\n   [1] It limits the damage before the threat spreads.\r\n   [2] It prevents all future incidents from occurring.\r\n   [3] It replaces the need for full containment steps.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Timely notification limits damage by letting security teams isolate the threat early, meets legal deadlines, preserves trust, and speeds recovery.\r\n\r\n### ch5-q18\r\n Q: Which action belongs to containing an incident?\r\n   [0] Restoring all critical data from the verified backups.\r\n   [1] Disconnecting compromised devices to stop movement.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [2] Reviewing the lessons learned after an incident.\r\n   [3] Drafting the final breach report for management.\r\n EXP: Containment includes isolating affected systems, disabling compromised accounts, applying short-term fixes, and preserving evidence.\r\n\r\n","metadata":{"output":"### ch1-q10\r\n Q: In the reference example, what missing item did the audit team address during the exit interview?\r\n   [0] The finance team's reconciled cash position for the quarter.\r\n   [1] The IT department's access control and user log reports.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [2] The network team's revised firewall policy for servers.\r\n   [3] The HR department's hiring records.\r\n EXP: The example shows the audit team identifying that the IT department had not submitted its latest access-control review or user-permission logs, then asking who will provide them and establishing a deadline.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q23\r\n Q: In Step 5, what does interpreting the results require the analyst to determine?\r\n   [0] Which raw files should be deleted after the analysis step.\r\n   [1] What is being learned from the results of the analysis.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [2] Which software performed the analysis fastest.\r\n   [3] Which metrics were collected during Step 2.\r\n EXP: Step 5 asks what you are learning from the results so the insights can be applied to the business.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q24\r\n Q: Which item is a purpose of an audit report?\r\n   [0] Reducing the number of audit findings.\r\n   [1] Assigning blame for control failures.\r\n   [2] Documenting examined evidence.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [3] Automating the audit process.\r\n EXP: The purposes of an audit report include formal communication, documentation of evidence, and initiation of corrective action closure.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q37\r\n Q: Which quality of a good audit report is reflected by issuing the report promptly?\r\n   [0] Confidential.\r\n   [1] Objective.\r\n   [2] Constructive.\r\n   [3] Timeliness.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Timely means the report is issued promptly, one of the six qualities of a good audit report along with accurate, objective, clear, constructive, and confidential.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q39\r\n Q: Which is a disadvantage of presenting audit findings?\r\n   [0] It delays stakeholder acceptance.\r\n   [1] It removes important technical detail.\r\n   [2] It can oversimplify and cause misuse.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [3] It prevents discussion of matters in scope.\r\n EXP: Condensing detailed technical or financial data into summary slides can lead to oversimplification or takeaways taken out of context.\r\n\r\n### ch2-q01\r\n Q: What do security logs record?\r\n   [0] Activity on computers, networks, applications, and devices.\r\n   [1] Approved financial transactions made by senior management.\r\n   [2] The physical location of every employee each working day.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [3] Only the successful logins on a single host system.\r\n EXP: Security logs record activities occurring on computers, networks, applications, and security devices.\r\n\r\n### ch2-q17\r\n Q: How should logs be protected during transmission and storage?\r\n   [0] By encryption.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [1] By compression.\r\n   [2] By duplication.\r\n   [3] By isolation.\r\n EXP: Logs should be encrypted during transmission and storage.\r\n\r\n### ch5-q16\r\n Q: How does timely notification help an organization, per the reference?\r\n   [0] It increases the total recovery budget available.\r\n   [1] It limits the damage before the threat spreads.\r\n   [2] It prevents all future incidents from occurring.\r\n   [3] It replaces the need for full containment steps.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Timely notification limits damage by letting security teams isolate the threat early, meets legal deadlines, preserves trust, and speeds recovery.\r\n\r\n### ch5-q18\r\n Q: Which action belongs to containing an incident?\r\n   [0] Restoring all critical data from the verified backups.\r\n   [1] Disconnecting compromised devices to stop movement.  <--CORRECT\r\n   [2] Reviewing the lessons learned after an incident.\r\n   [3] Drafting the final breach report for management.\r\n EXP: Containment includes isolating affected systems, disabling compromised accounts, applying short-term fixes, and preserving evidence.\r\n\r\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"& \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python311\\python.exe\" \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\iasexam\\spotcheck.py\"","time":{"start":1789824114417,"end":1789824114801}},"id":"prt_0b9d49d80001kpGjNGn7t46gCy","sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","messageID":"msg_0b9d46e94001acAow10xv2NP4t"}}
