{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824149278,"sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_80a12ba80df24307807897df","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"& \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python311\\python.exe\" -c \"\nimport json\np = r'C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json'\ndoc = json.load(open(p, encoding='utf-8'))\nwant = {'ch1-q30','ch1-q31','ch1-q36'}\nfor c in doc['chapters']:\n    for q in c['questions']:\n        if q['id'] in want:\n            ca = q['correctAnswer']\n            print('###', q['id'])\n            print(' Q:', q['question'])\n            print('   [%d] %s  <--CORRECT' % (ca, q['choices'][ca]))\n            print(' EXP:', q['explanation'])\n            print()\n\""},"output":"### ch1-q30\r\n Q: Which quality of a good data analysis means the methodology could produce the same conclusions when repeated?\r\n   [0] Reproducible results.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Reproducible means the methodology is clear enough that another security professional could analyze the same raw data and reach the same conclusions.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q31\r\n Q: Which quality of a good exit interview keeps every statement grounded in verifiable logs or screenshots?\r\n   [2] Objective and evidence based.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Objective and evidence-based means every statement is grounded in verifiable logs, screenshots, or configuration files, never assumptions or personal opinions.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q36\r\n Q: In an audit finding, which component describes what was found or observed?\r\n   [2] Condition.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Condition describes what was found or observed, while criteria states what should have been in place, cause explains why the issue occurred, and effect or risk covers the possible impact.\r\n\r\n","metadata":{"output":"### ch1-q30\r\n Q: Which quality of a good data analysis means the methodology could produce the same conclusions when repeated?\r\n   [0] Reproducible results.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Reproducible means the methodology is clear enough that another security professional could analyze the same raw data and reach the same conclusions.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q31\r\n Q: Which quality of a good exit interview keeps every statement grounded in verifiable logs or screenshots?\r\n   [2] Objective and evidence based.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Objective and evidence-based means every statement is grounded in verifiable logs, screenshots, or configuration files, never assumptions or personal opinions.\r\n\r\n### ch1-q36\r\n Q: In an audit finding, which component describes what was found or observed?\r\n   [2] Condition.  <--CORRECT\r\n EXP: Condition describes what was found or observed, while criteria states what should have been in place, cause explains why the issue occurred, and effect or risk covers the possible impact.\r\n\r\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"& \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python311\\python.exe\" -c \"\nimport json\np = r'C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\enaxqoqxb74s4g\\questions.json'\ndoc = json.load(open(p, encoding='utf-8'))\nwant = {'ch1-q30','ch1-q31','ch1-q36'}\nfor c in doc['chapters']:\n    for q in c['questions']:\n        if q['id'] in want:\n            ca = q['correctAnswer']\n            print('###', q['id'])\n            print(' Q:', q['question'])\n            print('   [%d] %s  <--CORRECT' % (ca, q['choices'][ca]))\n            print(' EXP:', q['explanation'])\n            print()\n\"","time":{"start":1789824148893,"end":1789824149228}},"id":"prt_0b9d51e74001b18c5aUGIZvYQB","sessionID":"ses_f464447b3ffe6otWPhKUxoCp1k","messageID":"msg_0b9d4a0970019nakkSxpldNQCB"}}
